  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 49922f05034be6f4fa205a70b2ad0a2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: C_P_Programs
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodexPageData
  Title: Programs
  Version: 1.0.0
  Icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 78447f4bcee6ac84f9a8f18f0f2ee53e, type: 3}
  TagLine: '"Technology!"'
  ContentHeaders:
  - Lore Entry
  Content:
  - "Programs are the way we can make you stronger.\n\nYou might not be able to hold
    run all of them at once, but I'd take a guess and say that if you plan which
    ones you do run together, you might be able to find some interesting combinations.
    \n\nI know they all don't seem overly useful compared to each other. But just
    think about this. They get crazier the more you go. And sometimes? That extra
    15% damage might be more helpful than letting some memory go to waste because
    you can't fit another physics breaking app into your memory.\n\nI should also
    mention the power of Application Suites. All apps are broken into groups we call
    \"Suites\". When enough are run in parallel, latent code of some sci-fi jargon
    happens and you gain a substantial secondary effect. Supposedly, their really
    powerful if you manage to get them all. Activation criteria and effects may differ,
    contact your mechanic imediately if you experience any negative symptoms.\n\nJust
    do us all a favor. Don't destroy the world with this power. And if you do? I
    won't look at your crash report. You can just take the win."
